# How to add to this file:
#
#   * Anchor with a leading "/" unless the rule genuinely has to match at
#     every depth. An unanchored prefix glob is how a source file ends up
#     invisible in a fresh clone while still working on the machine that
#     wrote it: `test*` used to hide frontend/src/lib/testing/ and
#     frontend/src/testing.d.ts, and CI failed on imports that resolve fine
#     locally.
#   * Never glob over a name source files might share (test, spec, config,
#     coverage) without anchoring it to the exact place the junk appears.
#   * Comments go on their own line. Git treats a trailing "#" as part of
#     the pattern.
#
# scripts/check-gitignore.sh (make check-gitignore, and a CI job) enforces
# the two invariants that keep this honest: no tracked file may match a rule
# here, and no source file may be ignored.

# Editors and OS
**/.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Node and pnpm
node_modules/
/.pnpm-store/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
/pnpm-audit-results.json

# Built frontend assets, embedded by server/frontend (//go:embed all:dist/*).
# Nothing here is tracked: the filenames are content hashes, so committing
# them would churn on every rebuild. `make frontend` produces them, and it is
# a prerequisite of building or testing the Go side at all. The tracked
# placeholder keeps the directory itself present, so the embed pattern always
# has somewhere to look.
/server/frontend/dist/*
!/server/frontend/dist/.gitignore

# Compiled output
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
# `go test -c`, or a test binary left behind by an interrupted run
*.test
# delve
**/__debug_*
# `make cross-compile-verify` builds these straight into the repo root
/ssoossh
/ssoosshd
# `make server-linux-build-local`: mirrors the linux/$TARGETARCH/ssoosshd
# layout goreleaser's docker build context has, for a local `docker build .`
# / `docker compose build` against Dockerfile or Dockerfile.musl.
/linux/
# goreleaser, and the macOS signing tool it shells out to
/dist/
/quill
# `make pam`: pam_ssoossh.so plus the cgo header goreleaser generates
/.build/

# Local runtime state and config. Named exactly, not globbed: `ssoossh*.yaml`
# would swallow any sample or example config added later. Name local variants
# *.local.yaml (ignored below).
/ssoossh.db*
/ssoossh.yaml
/ssoosshd.yaml
/ssl/
/.data/
/downloads/

# Secrets and environment. The root .env is tracked (it holds a local `act`
# alias, nothing secret), hence the one negation; everything else, templates
# included, stays local.
.env*
!/.env
.secrets
/.envrc
/private.pgp

# Coverage and test artifacts.
/coverage*
/.coverage/
# Runtime diagnostics a failing run leaves behind. Every suite built on
# test/e2e/harness writes them next to its own package (artifactsRoot in
# harness/artifacts.go), so this covers test/e2e, test/load, test/resilience
# and any suite added later.
/test/*/_artifacts/

# Generated at release time by scripts/gen-third-party-licenses.sh
/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md

# Agent and local tooling state. Only .claude/rules is shared; settings.json,
# hooks/, and skills/ stay local until someone deliberately un-ignores them.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/rules/
/CLAUDE.md
/.claudeignore
/.rtk/
/devcontainer-lock.json
*.local.sh
*.local.yml
*.local.yaml


# Personal scratch list. Untracked deliberately: it is a working note, and
# tracking it turns every reordering into a diff for everyone else.
/todo.md
